# serializer version: 1
# name: test_phase1_appends_lifecycle_suffixes_for_pending_snippets
  '''
  # PHASE 1: Snippet Index (IDs + descriptions)
  # Review the snippets below and select the IDs you need.
  # Filter with --areas <principle|concept|policy|procedure|design|spec|adr> and/or --domains <software-development|creative|marketing|customer-relations> (omit for all)
  
  project/spec/feature/context/current-snippet: A current snippet with no pending state.
  project/spec/feature/context/pending-snippet: A pending snippet owned by two slugs.  (delivered by: slug-a, slug-b)
  project/spec/feature/context/superseded-snippet: A current snippet with an in-flight change.  (superseded by: slug-c)
  
  # ⚠️  IMPORTANT: Call `telec docs get` again with the snippet IDs of interest!
  
  # NOTE: Pending work is flagged inline, never hidden: `(delivered by: slug)` marks a
  # not-yet-live NEW snippet; `(superseded by: slug)` marks a LIVE snippet with an incoming
  # rework (companion file or planned section). The bodies stay invisible until active —
  # `telec docs get` strips planned sections; `telec docs get <id> --target <slug>` reveals them.
  # `telec docs index --target <slug>` focuses on one todo's new snippets.
  '''
# ---
# name: test_phase2_non_owning_target_keeps_matching_companion_invisible
